# Orthogonally-decoupled IMDP, dims 2x2 (states (i,j), linearised s = i + 2j, dim 0 fastest).
# Single action; per-dimension marginal interval distributions. Target = (1,1) = state 3,
# absorbing. Oracle: IntervalMDP.jl OrthogonalIntervalMarkovDecisionProcess on the SAME
# model (peers/odimdp_oracle.jl).
odimdp
dims 2 2
init 0
label target 3
# state 0 = (0,0)
otran 0 0 0 0:0.3:0.7 1:0.3:0.7
otran 0 0 1 0:0.4:0.6 1:0.4:0.6
# state 1 = (1,0)
otran 1 0 0 0:0.0:0.2 1:0.8:1.0
otran 1 0 1 0:0.5:0.5 1:0.5:0.5
# state 2 = (0,1) DEAD (absorbing, not target -> mass here is lost)
otran 2 0 0 0:1:1
otran 2 0 1 1:1:1
# state 3 = (1,1) target, absorbing
otran 3 0 0 1:1:1
otran 3 0 1 1:1:1
